Package: pve-qnap-plugin
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: pve-qnap-plugin contributors <noreply@example.com>
Depends: libpve-storage-perl (>= 8.0), libjson-perl, libwww-perl, liblwp-protocol-https-perl, open-iscsi
Homepage: https://github.com/yacchi/pve-qnap-plugin
Description: QNAP NAS storage plugin for Proxmox VE
 Uses a QNAP NAS (QuTS hero / QTS) as block storage for Proxmox VE.
 Each VM disk maps to one QNAP volume (zvol) exported as an iSCSI LUN.
 .
 Snapshots, rollback and clones are performed by the NAS itself, so
 snapshots do not depend on qcow2 and linked clones are copy-on-write:
 instant and near zero space.
